# Newsletter System Environment Variables
# Updated for Vercel Blob Cloud Storage (Production Ready)

# ===========================================
# EMAIL CONFIGURATION (Required)
# ===========================================
# Your Gmail email address
EMAIL_USER=your-email@gmail.com

# Gmail App Password (NOT your regular password)
# Generate this from: https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
# Steps:
# 1. Go to Google Account settings
# 2. Security tab
# 3. 2-Step Verification (must be enabled)
# 4. App passwords
# 5. Generate app password for "Mail"
EMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=your-app-password-here

# Example:
# EMAIL_USER=kibeenock7390@gmail.com
# EMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=abcd efgh ijkl mnop

# ===========================================
# VERCEL BLOB STORAGE (Production Ready)
# ===========================================
# This replaces the old file-based storage that had read-only issues in production
# Automatically created when you set up Vercel Blob in your dashboard

# Vercel Blob Read/Write Token
# This is automatically generated by Vercel when you create a Blob store
# Steps to get this:
# 1. Go to your Vercel project dashboard
# 2. Click "Storage" tab
# 3. Click "Connect Database" → "Blob"
# 4. Name: newsletter-subscribers (or any name)
# 5. Select all environments (dev/preview/prod)
# 6. This token will be auto-created as BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=vercel_blob_rw_xxxxxxxxxx

# ===========================================
# MIGRATION NOTES
# ===========================================
# BEFORE (Had Issues):
# - Used local file storage: data/subscribers.json
# - Worked in development only
# - FAILED in production with: "EROFS: read-only file system"
# - Data lost on each deployment

# AFTER (Current Solution):
# - Uses Vercel Blob cloud storage
# - Works in development AND production
# - Data persists across deployments
# - Auto-scaling and reliable
# - No file system limitations

# ===========================================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# ===========================================
# 1. Email Setup:
#    - Set EMAIL_USER and EMAIL_APP_PASSWORD above
# 2. Vercel Blob Setup:
#    - Create Blob store in Vercel dashboard
#    - Run: vercel env pull (to get BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN)
# 3. Test:
#    - npm run dev (local testing)
#    - vercel --prod (production deployment)
